From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 05:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lib: hexdump: keep print_hex_dump_bytes exported with dynamic debug

With CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG=y, include/linux/printk.h turns
print_hex_dump_bytes() into a dynamic_hex_dump() macro and lib/hexdump.c
compiles the real function out.  Vendor-built wireless modules - the
ATBM6062CU blob, among others - link against the plain symbol, so enabling
dynamic debug for a board makes them fail to load with

    atbm606x_bt_usb: Unknown symbol print_hex_dump_bytes

Undefine the macro in hexdump.c and always build and export the function.
In-tree callers keep using the macro, so dynamic-debug behaviour is
unchanged; only the exported symbol is restored for out-of-tree modules.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
 lib/hexdump.c | 13 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/hexdump.c b/lib/hexdump.c
--- a/lib/hexdump.c
+++ b/lib/hexdump.c
@@ -227,7 +227,16 @@
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(print_hex_dump);
 
-#if !defined(CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG)
+#if defined(CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG)
+/*
+ * printk.h replaces print_hex_dump_bytes() with a dynamic_hex_dump() macro
+ * when dynamic debug is enabled. Vendor-built modules still link against the
+ * plain symbol, so undefine the macro here and keep exporting the function.
+ * In-tree callers keep using the macro; only the exported symbol is restored.
+ */
+#undef print_hex_dump_bytes
+#endif
+
 /**
  * print_hex_dump_bytes - shorthand form of print_hex_dump() with default params
  * @prefix_str: string to prefix each line with;
@@ -247,5 +256,4 @@
 		       buf, len, true);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(print_hex_dump_bytes);
-#endif /* !defined(CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG) */
 #endif /* defined(CONFIG_PRINTK) */
